## Access Rules

- Do not copy private wiki content into this repo.
- Public memory is a derived surface; private or local-only bodies can only move upward as approved facts, redacted summaries, or abstracted non-reversible conclusions.
- If an area is private, state the access boundary and ask the owner for approved extracts.
- Read `identity/memories/wiki-repo.yml` before assuming whether GitHub or server wiki is authoritative.
- If server wiki is authoritative, treat GitHub as a mirror/collaboration surface and prefer server state for facts.
- Use the memory wiki `query` section to find the configured entrypoint and area index. If the wiki is unavailable, fall back to memory tiers and ask the owner for an approved extract.
- Use the memory wiki `intake` section before writing new material. Raw bodies stay external; this repo receives approved summaries, source IDs, provenance, and distilled conclusions.
- Prefer latest memory source over older PSP facts for time-sensitive work context.
- Treat unprocessed thought intake as provisional, not stable fact.
- This first stage has no personal evidence body. It only defines where future owner-approved evidence will enter the system.
